      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm trying to run this macro for our monthly reconciliation but it keeps crashing. i keep getting \"Run-time error '1004': Application-defined or object-defined error\" right when it tries to copy the data from the temp sheet to the master sheet. can u look at the code and see whats wrong?\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsTemp As Worksheet\n    Dim wsMaster As Worksheet\n    Set wsTemp = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"TempData\")\n    Set wsMaster = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Master\")\n    \n    ' attempting to copy range A1:G50\n    wsTemp.Range(\"A1:G50\").Copy\n    wsMaster.Range(\"A1\").PasteSpecial Paste:=xlPasteValues\n    \n    MsgBox \"Reconciliation Complete\"\nEnd Sub",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The error occurs because using `.Copy` creates a temporary clipboard reference that may conflict with the workbook's state, especially in macro-enabled workbooks. It's often more reliable to use `Copy` followed by `Cut`, or better yet, assign ranges directly using assignments or `.Range.Value` to avoid copy-paste copy-paste overhead. Additionally, ensure the names \"TempData\" and \"Master\" exist and the temp sheet isn't protected before running this.",
